WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.969
-Our first guest tonight is an
Emmy and Golden Globe winning

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:05.304
comedian you know from his work
on "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:08.308
Palm Springs, and is one third
of The Lonely Island.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:10.543
He stars in "Brooklyn 99,"
which returns tomorrow night

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.745
at 8 for it's final season
right here on NBC.

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:14.280
Please welcome back to the show
our very good friend

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.815
Andy Samberg.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:21.287
-Oh, uh, actually, Seth, yeah,
I'm trying a new character.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:24.690
-You're trying a new character?
-Yeah, it's a new character.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.759
It's really good,
can you just read the card

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:32.432
you're about to be handed?

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:35.034
-And now,
here with a health update,

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:38.905
please welcome esteemed
immunologist Dr. Faucberg.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:42.908
-[ Sighs ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:42.908 --> 00:00:46.378
-Hey, Seth,
what an honor to be here.

00:00:46.378 --> 00:00:50.016
-So, uh, Dr. Faucberg, is it
safe to say you're

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:54.020
no relation to Dr. Fauci?
-He's my fifth cousin.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.988
-Oh, really? I've never heard
of a fifth cousin.

00:00:55.988 --> 00:00:58.991
-Yeah, it's when only the start
of your last name is the same.

00:00:58.991 --> 00:01:00.793
-Uh-huh.
-Yeah, so, like,

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:03.663
famous fifth cousins would be.,
Bruce Springsteen

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.498
and Rick Springfield.
-Yeah.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:09.602
-Or Barack Obama and Steve-O.
-What?

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.604
-What? We can both say "what"
when the other person's

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.439
being crazy, Seth.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:16.009
Sorry to steal the go-to arrow
from your quiver.

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:25.385
-Okay, so. So, Dr. Faucberg --
-Dr. Andthony Faucberg, yes.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:28.721
-Your first name is "And"-thony?
-It is.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.990
I'm sixth cousins with
Andy Samberg

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.193
because our first names
start the same.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:37.997
-Dr. Andthony Faucberg,
is it safe to assume

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.866
you're here to talk to us about
the coronavirus?

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:44.303
-No, Seth. I'm here to talk to
you about a new virus.

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:46.639
A virus more deadly
than any we have ever seen

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.275
in the field of science or any
of the other fields.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:56.148
-The other fields?
-Wrigley, Sally, W.C.

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:59.118
-What's the new virus?

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:03.089
-The Frisbee virus.
-Oh, [Bleep] off, Andy.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:07.793
-Hey! Leave my cousin outta this
he has nothing to do with this.

00:02:07.793 --> 00:02:10.896
-What's, what's
the Frisbee virus?

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:13.499
-It's a matter of life and death
and it's easy to catch.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:15.135
-And how do you catch it?

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.736
-All you have to do is
take one look

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:19.172
at your ugly-ass dog Frisbee
and you know you have it

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:22.208
if you throw up right away.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.742
-Which is why,
if you think you're at risk

00:02:23.742 --> 00:02:26.346
of seeing a Frisbee,
you have to mask up.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:27.913
Let me show you the proper
technique.

00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:30.450
-Okay.
-Just like that.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.853
You see, Seth?
You see how it works?

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.422
This is what you do when you
don't want to see Frisbee.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.991
-Are you gonna keep that mask on
for the rest of the interview?

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:41.594
-Uh, no. I am not, because I
have not memorized this script.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:44.830
It's hot off the presses.
-How -- How did

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:49.068
the Frisbee virus start?
-Ah, good setup question, Seth,

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.136
thank you.

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:52.237
She was either purchased
at a wet market,

00:02:52.237 --> 00:02:54.173
which makes sense,
because she looks like a wet rat

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:58.177
or she was created in a lab,
which also makes sense,

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:00.513
because no god would make such
a foul creature.

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.549
-Sure. Sure.
-Next question of course

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:05.285
would be did she escape
from a lab?

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:07.887
-Yeah.
-I don't think that's likely.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.922
-You don't think that's likely?
-No.

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:12.292
I think it's more likely that
someone who worked at the lab

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:14.626
said this dog sucks,
we should let her out,

00:03:14.626 --> 00:03:16.361
and then say she escaped.

00:03:16.361 --> 00:03:18.564
And then everyone agreed to that
plan because, you know.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:22.635
[ Sniffs ] She sucks.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.770
-Are we done?
-Wait, hold on, hold on!

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:28.641
Uh, let me see. Oh, you need a
super strong vaccine

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.442
for the Frisbee virus,
because she suck so much.

00:03:30.442 --> 00:03:32.344
-Uh-huh.
-Yeah, it's like way stronger

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:33.679
than Johnson &amp; Johnson.
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:35.414
But do you want to know what
vaccine is way stronger

00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:37.517
than Johnson &amp; Johnson?
-No.

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:39.051
Dwayne "The Rock"
Johnson &amp; Johnson.

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:40.586
Did that work with the crew,
Seth?

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:42.522
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.590
-Just let me know if that played
with the crew.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.726
I'm dying to know.
-I think we can probably

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.961
wrap this up now.
-Yeah.

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:51.864
Uh, when they play me on "SNL"
I wanted it to Clooney.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.198
I know that you're allowed to
call it now,

00:03:53.198 --> 00:03:55.034
so I want it to be Clooney.
-Please give it up

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.903
for Dr. Andthony Faucberg.

00:03:57.903 --> 00:03:59.806
We'll be right back
with Andy Samberg.

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:00.873
-My cousin!

